 of daily living for any resident who is unable.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0803":{"code":"F-0803","title":"Ensure menus must meet the nutritional needs of residents, be prepared in advance, be followed, be updated, be reviewed by dietician, and meet the needs of the resident.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0804":{"code":"F-0804","title":"Ensure food and drink is palatable, attractive, and at a safe and appetizing temperature.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0908":{"code":"F-0908","title":"Keep all essential equipment working safely.","category":"Environmental Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0921":{"code":"F-0921","title":"Make sure that the nursing home area is safe, easy to use, clean and comfortable for residents, staff and the public.","category":"Environmental Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0583":{"code":"F-0583","title":"Keep residents' personal and medical records private and confidential.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0584":{"code":"F-0584","title":"Honor the resident's right to a safe, clean, comfortable and homelike environment, including but not limited to receiving treatment and supports for daily living safely.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0600":{"code":"F-0600","title":"Protect each resident from all types of abuse such as physical, mental, sexual abuse, physical punishment, and neglect by anybody.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0609":{"code":"F-0609","title":"Timely report suspected abuse, neglect, or theft and report the results of the investigation to proper authorities.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0610":{"code":"F-0610","title":"Respond appropriately to all alleged violations.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0684":{"code":"F-0684","title":"Provide appropriate treatment and care according to orders, resident’s preferences and goals.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0686":{"code":"F-0686","title":"Provide appropriate pressure ulcer care and prevent new ulcers from developing.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0689":{"code":"F-0689","title":"Ensure that a nursing home area is free from accident hazards and provides adequate supervision to prevent accidents.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0690":{"code":"F-0690","title":"Provide appropriate care for residents who are continent or incontinent of bowel/bladder, appropriate catheter care,  and appropriate care  to prevent urinary tract infections.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0693":{"code":"F-0693","title":"Ensure that feeding tubes are  not used unless there is a medical reason and the resident agrees; and provide appropriate care for a resident with a feeding tube.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0755":{"code":"F-0755","title":"Provide pharmaceutical services to meet the needs of each resident and employ or obtain the services of a licensed pharmacist.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0756":{"code":"F-0756","title":"Ensure a licensed pharmacist perform a monthly drug regimen review, including the medical chart, following irregularity reporting guidelines in developed policies and procedures.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0760":{"code":"F-0760","title":"Ensure that residents are free from significant medication errors.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0880":{"code":"F-0880","title":"Provide and implement an infection prevention and control program.","category":"Infection Control Deficiencies","concept":"infection_prevention","concept_label":"Infection prevention"},"cms-f0676":{"code":"F-0676","title":"Ensure residents do not lose the ability to perform activities of daily living unless there is a medical reason.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0559":{"code":"F-0559","title":"Honor the resident's right to share a room with spouse or roommate of choice and receive written notice before a change is made.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/ne